{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Peer-push overlays: a library pushed from a peer (dev.dev.install_lib) into a data/<lib> that is a symlink into a git checkout is written through the link, leaving the checkout dirty on purpose - a tentative build being tested outside git. The instance-local marker runtime/dev/peer_overlays.json {lib: {lib, peer, peer_name, version, repo_path, rel, head, hash, time}} records it. While a marker stands, dev.git.autocommit_sweep and agent.committer.sweep_repo leave the whole repo uncommitted (result peer_overlay) and dev.git.repo_state names it; dev.github.update and dev.git.update_from_master restore it before pulling/merging. op: list (repo and/or lib filter, \"\" = all; returns {count, overlays}); mark (lib + entry with repo_path and rel; a second push keeps the first head); forget (drop markers, files untouched); restore (repo and/or lib: git checkout HEAD -- <rel> and clean -fd -- <rel>, plus the crate's generated <root>/src/<lib>, cmdinit.rs and lib.rs when the repo carries the crate; drops the marker; returns {restored:[{lib, peer, removed (app files the push shipped that git does not), rust}], steps, errors} - anything edited in that library on this box since the push is discarded with it); install (lib + entry {removed, rust, activate}: dev.dev.refresh_apps then dev.dev.activate_lib, the forced re-install after a restore; returns {steps, restart, apps, activate}). repo is a registered repo name or a path. Pass {} for entry when unused. Returns FLAT.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};","params":[{"name":"op","type":"String"},{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"entry","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ktslky1a1fba9bd72u1","readers":[],"time":1795224953853,"username":"system","writers":[]}